{"author":"rebar-bridge[bot]","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"compacted_at":1793427366701469722,"compiled_state":{"alias":"trilateral-prosperous-cusimanse","assignee":null,"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","authorship":{"signed":4,"unsigned":0},"authorship_ledger":[{"content_hash":"d17dbab2dd3869175dd152fd3abc992d0b5d5f6315e10aa6687640c07ca549a2","event_uuid":"b665d58a-20c2-4cce-bf63-24056a4dfd65","position":{"commit_sha":"5d3bff92a878919bd06b9fc67c4d8fb98f4ab1b3","position":"1793420932060265373-b665d58a-20c2-4cce-bf63-24056a4dfd65"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"3cdf4d8657daa2e7147a672aa58f0a0485e7a42a8551a39b0a0b67e57129a1ae","event_uuid":"1fab512f-90c1-4206-8514-c33f4fb15f75","position":{"commit_sha":"bff790e8c78f1b60019f9703bf91903b609db563","position":"1793420942140847810-1fab512f-90c1-4206-8514-c33f4fb15f75"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"37489cbdb4b59d3e054d77afbaeed16b85f56e82e1e695cc240cc840443ff3f9","event_uuid":"17233c2a-27d8-4c79-a21e-8f789a63187a","position":{"commit_sha":"4f14dcdf6986f5b3849d54c082d5b32dcc294377","position":"1793421219036466786-17233c2a-27d8-4c79-a21e-8f789a63187a"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"13e6f42e1b708bdb79e5f244166c17636869b8e43e60b66c4aaebb36a9eb016b","event_uuid":"97945f44-50e7-4e1a-a482-67ab8a5979a4","position":{"commit_sha":"49ee286d1bfa9686fb6bb73c0a32cc9997558ac6","position":"1793421789135917366-97945f44-50e7-4e1a-a482-67ab8a5979a4"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Fourth verified instance, and the first caught **before** review rather than after — `cb2b-7446-748c-47bc`, swept against current `origin/main`.\n\nIts AC1 requires `git grep -n '_ALIASES\\b\\|_LEGACY_ENV_ALIASES\\|_map_legacy_env' -- src tests scripts` to return empty. It cannot, on any correct implementation. Two independent reasons, both of the class this bug describes:\n\n1. **Regex over-match.** `\\b` anchors the end of the identifier, so `_ALIASES\\b` also matches the tail of unrelated live names: `_ARCH_ALIASES` (`scripts/ensure_pandoc.py:50,94`), `_HIDDEN_ALIASES` and `_REMOVED_SIMPLE_CLI_ALIASES` (`src/rebar/_cli/_help_route.py:31,64,183,186,190`, `_cli/_registry.py:565`), `_EDIT_FLAG_ALIASES` (`_commands/composer_edit.py:210,388`), `_DEPRECATED_PROVIDER_ALIASES` (`llm/providers.py:32,64`), plus 6 test modules referencing `_HIDDEN_ALIASES`. 19 hits the story must not touch.\n\n2. **Prose the deletion cannot reach.** `tests/unit/test_config_surface_golden.py:177` is a docstring narrating that `_env_signature` *used to* read `_LEGACY_ENV_ALIASES` — correct as written and not a defect. `tests/fixtures/cloud_adf_corpus/bodies_00.json` and `tests/fixtures/dc_wiki_corpus/table.json` contain `_map_legacy_env` inside captured ticket-body prose used as bridge-rendering fixtures; editing them would corrupt the fixtures.\n\nThe same sweep also found that `_LEGACY_ENV_ALIASES` and `_map_legacy_env` are **already absent from `src/`**, so one of the plan's enumerated deletion targets no longer exists — the enumeration is wrong in both directions at once, naming a path with nothing to delete while missing paths that carry hits.\n\nThis instance sharpens the proposed check in two ways the first three did not:\n\n- A grep-shaped AC needs its **regex** validated against the tree, not just its path list. An AC that over-matches is as unsatisfiable as one that under-enumerates, and the failure looks identical at close time.\n- The sweep must distinguish **code references from prose references**. Docstrings recording history and captured-text fixtures legitimately retain a deleted symbol's name forever. A check that flags them as omissions would be noise, so path exclusions (`tests/fixtures`) and a prose/code distinction belong in the design.\n\nBoth reinforce AC1 and AC2 as written rather than changing them; recording here so the implementer has a concrete fixture to build against.","timestamp":1793421219036466786},{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"## Fifth verified instance — `596b-919d-8d2a-404a` AC2\n\nSame shape as the dc42 and 25a4 instances: a grep-shaped AC whose required-empty result is defeated by a site the plan's own Approach never enumerates.\n\nAC2 requires this to be empty:\n\n```\ngit grep -n 'REBAR_CANARY_HEARTBEAT_SOURCE\\|github-api' -- scripts .github tests\n```\n\nThe Approach enumerates `tests/scripts/test_canary_bridge_heldout.py:74,145` and \"delete `:163-174`\". The live tree has a fourth hit in that file at `:122`:\n\n```python\nenv = hb_env(tmp_path, REBAR_CANARY_HEARTBEAT_SOURCE=\"status\")\n```\n\n**The miss has a legible cause, and it sharpens the design.** The story is about retiring the `github-api` rollback *value*. Every site the author enumerated passes `github-api`. This one passes `\"status\"` — the value being *kept* — so it does not look implicated when scanning for the thing being removed. But the AC greps the **variable name** as well as the value, so a site using the surviving value still fails it.\n\nThat is a distinct failure mode from the earlier four, and worth stating in AC5's guidance separately: **when a grep-shaped AC matches on more than one alternation branch, the enumeration has to be done per branch.** Enumerating against the branch that motivates the story silently drops every site that matches only the other branch. A mechanical check — run the AC's grep verbatim and diff its hit set against the plan's enumerated sites — catches this class without the author needing to notice the asymmetry.\n\n## Counter-evidence worth recording\n\nIn the same sweep, 596b's AC2 grep was checked for the *over*-matching failure mode (the `cb2b` instance, where `_ALIASES\\b` matched 19 unrelated symbols). It does not over-match: `github-api` is a sufficiently specific token that all 14 live hits are genuinely in scope. So the two failure modes are independent — a plan can get the regex precision right and still under-enumerate, and vice versa. AC5's proposed check must cover both directions, which the \"diff the AC's own grep output against the enumerated set\" formulation does naturally.\n\n## Running instance count\n\n5 verified against the tree: dc42 (`docs/research/…:167`), dc42 (`test_plan_review_prerequisites_continuation_heldout.py` wholesale), 25a4 (AC8 5-vs-6 paths), cb2b (AC1 regex over-match), 596b (AC2 per-branch under-enumeration). All five were found by sweeping the AC's own command across the whole tree rather than by reading the plan.","timestamp":1793421789135917366}],"created_at":1793420932060265373,"creation_channel":"mcp","deps":[{"link_uuid":"1fab512f-90c1-4206-8514-c33f4fb15f75","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"25a4-1ab3-3558-4cd4"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\n\nA plan that passes `review-plan` can still enumerate a file set that is **smaller than\nthe one its own work compels**. The gate certifies the plan's reasoning; it does not\nsweep the tree to confirm the enumeration is closed under the change's own\nconsequences. So a certified plan can carry an acceptance criterion it is structurally\nincapable of satisfying, and nobody learns until implementation.\n\nThe failure is quiet in the worst way: the plan is certified, the author trusts the\nenumeration, and the gap surfaces either as a self-contradicting AC at close time or\nas an implementation that silently exceeds its reviewed scope.\n\n## Observation (measured)\n\nThree instances, all verified against the tree rather than recalled:\n\n**1. `dc42` — a plan whose own AC its file list could not satisfy.**\nAC1 required `grep -r fidelity_spot_eval src docs` to return no hits. The plan's file\nenumeration omitted `docs/research/task-decomposition-sota-2026.md`, which cited\n`fidelity_spot_eval` at line 167 as a working batch-rerun seam. With that hit present\nAC1 could never pass, so the plan as certified was unsatisfiable. The landed commit\n`e2ed08b343a` does touch that file, confirming the omission was real and compelled.\n\n**2. `dc42` — a module-wide deletion planned as a single-test deletion.**\nThe plan named one test in `tests/unit/test_plan_review_prerequisites_continuation_heldout.py`.\nThe module-level import is shared by all 4 tests and 3 of them call into the deleted\nmodule, so the whole file had to go. `e2ed08b343a` deletes it wholesale: 127 deletions,\n0 insertions.\n\n**3. `25a4` — an AC enumerating 5 paths where 6 are compelled.**\nAC8 lists 5 paths. `tests/unit/test_gen_env_registry.py:67`\n(`test_check_mode_clean_against_committed_tree`) asserts `gen.main([\"--check\"]) == 0`,\nwhich requires the committed `docs/env-vars.md` to match generator output. Any change\nto the env-var reads therefore compels regenerating that doc, making the true set 6.\nThe landed commit `e096a33d3b7` touches 6 paths. The AC is unsatisfiable as written and\nis currently blocking that ticket's close.\n\nA wider pattern was suspected across more tickets. That broader count is **unverified**\nand is deliberately not claimed here.\n\nWhat distinguishes all three from ordinary plan drift: the omitted file is not\nincidental, it is *forced* by the change the plan already describes. A per-symbol sweep\nof the whole tree finds them; sampling citations does not. In instance 1 that distinction\nis exactly what was observed — sampling passed, the sweep found the hit.\n\n## Approach (direction, not a committed design)\n\nGive plan review a mechanical closure check to complement its reasoning: for the symbols\na plan says it removes or renames, sweep the tree and compare the resulting hit set\nagainst the plan's enumerated paths, reporting any path that carries a hit but is not\nenumerated. The same sweep catches a test module whose surviving tests depend on a\ndeleted import.\n\nWhether this belongs as a new blocking criterion, an advisory finding, or a\npreflight the author runs before requesting review is for the implementer to determine.\nAn advisory finding is the cheaper first step and does not risk blocking correct plans\non an imprecise sweep.\n\n## Scope\n\n- The check's home (criterion, advisory finding, or author-run preflight) is open.\n- Tests covering a plan whose enumeration is closed and one whose enumeration is not.\n- Documentation of the check wherever plan-review criteria are described.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] AC1: Given a plan that names a symbol for removal and enumerates a file set that\n      omits a tree path carrying that symbol, the review output names the omitted path.\n- [ ] AC2: Given a plan whose enumeration already covers every path carrying the named\n      symbols, no such finding is emitted.\n- [ ] AC3: Given a plan that deletes a module and names only one test in a test file\n      whose module-level import binds that module, the review output identifies the\n      remaining tests in that file as affected.\n- [ ] AC4: The check is documented alongside the other plan-review criteria, and\n      `rebar explain` resolves it if it is registered as a criterion.\n- [ ] AC5: New tests cover AC1, AC2 and AC3 and are red before the change.\n- [ ] AC6: `make verify` exits 0, and the Gerrit change carries `LLM-Review +1` and\n      `Verified +1`.","env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","file_impact":[],"file_impact_scope":"undeclared","keyring":[],"managed_refs":[],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"open","tags":[],"ticket_id":"c9c2-c569-f5cb-426f","ticket_type":"bug","title":"Certified plans enumerate file sets their own work compels them to exceed","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["b665d58a-20c2-4cce-bf63-24056a4dfd65","1fab512f-90c1-4206-8514-c33f4fb15f75","17233c2a-27d8-4c79-a21e-8f789a63187a","97945f44-50e7-4e1a-a482-67ab8a5979a4"]},"env_id":"","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1793427366701469722,"uuid":"34e65e98-7fe5-4845-b467-47da66076c96"}